+# nl_shell.gate.commands; the format is described there. One engine
+# (nl_shell.gate.rules) reads every row; no command has a code path of its own.
+#
+# The rules every row is held to (spec §4.1):
+# - argv is always parsed: an option a row does not declare is at least destructive
+#   ("option the gate does not know"), and rejected on a row that elevates;
+# - every field that runs text names its grammar; text in a grammar the gate does not
+#   parse (python, perl, tcl, js, gdb, tmux, screen, gshell, unit, remote-sh) is
+#   decision B ("runs code the gate cannot read");
+# - a mode that runs a command, a script or stdin says what it does with no command
